# DclawOS 2.0 desktop: minimal X11 session (Openbox) + DclawOS shell.
# Deliberately NOT a full GNOME desktop: no gnome-shell, no gdm3, no
# gnome-control-center, no nautilus, no Firefox, no Office, no image/video
# viewers. The shell, dashboard, settings app and agent service are
# DclawOS-native and land module by module.
xorg
xauth
x11-xserver-utils
x11-utils
dbus-x11
policykit-1
lightdm
lightdm-gtk-greeter
openbox
python3
python3-gi
python3-websocket
gir1.2-gtk-3.0
gir1.2-wnck-3.0
# Phase 6 M5: GTK4 + libadwaita for the migrated windows
# (Debian Bookworm, verified on packages.debian.org/bookworm:
# gir1.2-gtk-4.0 4.8.3, gir1.2-adw-1 1.2.2 / libadwaita-1-0).
# The GTK3 typelibs above stay ONLY for the Wnck taskbar
# exception and dclawos-gui (docs/UI-FUNCTIONS.md).
gir1.2-gtk-4.0
gir1.2-adw-1
libadwaita-1-0
# Phase 6 M5: WebKitGTK 6.0 (GTK4) for the three WebView hosts
# (settings model page / chat / dashboard). Bookworm-verified:
# gir1.2-webkit-6.0 exists in bookworm (2.50.6-1~deb12u2 via
# bookworm-security; pulls libwebkitgtk-6.0-4). It REPLACES the
# M2-era gir1.2-webkit2-4.1 (GTK3) — the hosts are GTK4 now.
gir1.2-webkit-6.0
# Phase 6 M5: GtkSourceView 5 is the GTK4 generation of the
# editor's widget (Bookworm gir1.2-gtksource-5, 5.6.x); it
# replaces gir1.2-gtksource-4.
gir1.2-gtksource-5
libglib2.0-bin
upower
fonts-wqy-zenhei
xterm
xdotool
chromium
locales
# Livecd installer (Phase 3 module 5): Calamares + Debian settings,
# NOT a scripted installer (partitioning + bootloader + user setup
# stay tested code). Qt5 cost is a live-medium cost, not a feature cut.
calamares
calamares-settings-debian
qml-module-qtquick2
qml-module-qtquick-controls2
qml-module-qtquick-layouts
qml-module-qtquick-window2
